  {
    "id": "25366f00cee8279604ff",
    "source": "runtime:qa-help-spells-wounds",
    "context": "paragraph",
    "original": "All-round way to sacrifice something in order to please or thank the spirits and otherworldly beings in various occasions.",
    "translation": "适用于多种场合的献祭方式，用于取悦或感谢精灵与异界存在。",
    "status": "reviewed",
    "runtime_verified": true
  },
  {
    "id": "d48259cb250bc663096a",
    "source": "runtime:qa-help-spells-wounds",
    "context": "paragraph",
    "original": "After the bear is brought down its skull eventually needs to be placed to hang in a big lone pine-tree. That completes the hunting and burial ceremony and assures proper circulation of the bear spirit.",
    "translation": "猎杀熊之后，最终应将熊颅悬挂在一棵高大、独立的松树上。这样才算完成狩猎与葬礼仪式，确保熊之灵得到妥善的轮回。",
    "status": "reviewed",
    "runtime_verified": true
  },
  {
    "id": "488b345b2210d3e748fc",
    "source": "runtime:qa-help-spells-wounds",
    "context": "paragraph",
    "original": "Loop snares for hares shouldn't be set barehanded but you should always wear mittens, and preferably woollen mittens.",
    "translation": "设置捕兔绳套时不应赤手操作，而应始终戴着连指手套，最好使用羊毛连指手套。",
    "status": "reviewed",
    "runtime_verified": true
  },
  {
    "id": "ecc799ff0e8956322ab9",
    "source": "runtime:qa-help-spells-wounds",
    "context": "paragraph",
    "original": "Bear is a great hunter who always finds its prey, and hunters who carry bear teeth with them can come across hares and game birds as they please.",
    "translation": "熊是出色的猎手，总能找到猎物。随身携带熊牙的猎人，也能如愿遇见野兔和猎鸟。",
    "status": "reviewed",
    "runtime_verified": true
  },
